DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rreeaaddeellff utility displays information about ELF objects and ar(1) ar‐
     chives.

     The rreeaaddeellff utility recognizes the following options:

     --aa | ----aallll
             Turn on the following flags: --dd, --hh, --II, --ll, --nn, --rr, --ss, --uu, --AA,
             --SS and --VV.

     --cc | ----aarrcchhiivvee--iinnddeexx
             Print the archive symbol table for archives.

     --dd | ----ddyynnaammiicc
             Print the contents of the SHT_DYNAMIC sections in the ELF object.

     --ee | ----hheeaaddeerrss
             Print all program, file and section headers in the ELF object.

     --gg | ----sseeccttiioonn--ggrroouuppss
             Print the contents of the section groups in the ELF object.

     --hh | ----ffiillee--hheeaaddeerr
             Print the file header of the ELF object.

     --ll | ----pprrooggrraamm--hheeaaddeerrss
             Print the content of the program header table for the object.

     --nn | ----nnootteess
             Print the contents of PT_NOTE segments or SHT_NOTE sections
             present in the ELF object.

     --pp _s_e_c_t_i_o_n | ----ssttrriinngg--dduummpp=_s_e_c_t_i_o_n
             Print the contents of the specified section as printable strings.
             The argument _s_e_c_t_i_o_n should be the name of a section or a numeric
             section index.

     --rr | ----rreellooccss
             Print relocation information.

     --ss | ----ssyymmss | ----ssyymmbboollss
             Print symbol tables.

     --tt | ----sseeccttiioonn--ddeettaaiillss
             Print additional information about sections, such as the flags
             fields in section headers.  Implies --SS.

     --uu | ----uunnwwiinndd
             Not yet implemented (option accepted but ignored).

     --vv | ----vveerrssiioonn
             Prints a version identifier for rreeaaddeellff and exits.

     --ww[afilmoprsFLR] | ----ddeebbuugg--dduummpp[=_l_o_n_g_-_o_p_t_i_o_n_-_n_a_m_e,...]
             Display DWARF information.  The --ww option is used with the short
             options in the following table; the ----ddeebbuugg--dduummpp option is used
             with a comma-separated list of the corresponding long option
             names:

             _S_h_o_r_t _O_p_t_i_o_n    _L_o_n_g _O_p_t_i_o_n       _D_e_s_c_r_i_p_t_i_o_n
             a               abbrev            Show abbreviation information.
             f               frames            Show frame information,
                                               displaying frame instructions.
             i               info              Show debugging information
                                               entries.
             l               rawline           Show line information in raw
                                               form.
             m               macro             Show macro information.
             o               loc               Show location list information.
             p               pubnames          Show global names.
             r               aranges|ranges    Show address range information.
             s               str               Show the debug string table.
             F               frames-interp     Show frame information,
                                               displaying register rules.
             L               decodedline       Show line information in
                                               decoded form.
             R               Ranges            Show range lists.

             If no sub-options are specified, the default is to show informa‐
             tion corresponding to the _a, _f, _i_, _l, _o, _p, _r, _s and _R short op‐
             tions.

     --xx _s_e_c_t_i_o_n | ----hheexx--dduummpp=_s_e_c_t_i_o_n
             Display the contents of the specified section in hexadecimal.
             The argument _s_e_c_t_i_o_n should be the name of a section or a numeric
             section index.

     --zz | ----ddeeccoommpprreessss
             Decompress contents of sections specified by --xx or --pp before dis‐
             playing.  If the specified section is not compressed, it is dis‐
             played as is.

     --AA | ----aarrcchh--ssppeecciiffiicc
             This option is accepted but is currently unimplemented.

     --DD | ----uussee--ddyynnaammiicc
             Print the symbol table specified by the DT_SYMTAB entry in the
             “.dynamic” section.

     --HH | ----hheellpp
             Print a help message.

     --II | ----hhiissttooggrraamm
             Print information on bucket list lengths for sections of type
             SHT_HASH and SHT_GNU_HASH.

     --NN | ----ffuullll--sseeccttiioonn--nnaammee
             This option is accepted but is currently unimplemented.

     --SS | ----sseeccttiioonnss | ----sseeccttiioonn--hheeaaddeerrss
             Print information in the section headers for each ELF object.

     --VV | ----vveerrssiioonn--iinnffoo
             Print symbol versioning information.

     --WW | ----wwiiddee
             Print information about ELF structures using one long line per
             structure.  If this option is not specified, rreeaaddeellff will list
             information in the headers of 64 bit ELF objects on two separate
             lines.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The rreeaaddeellff utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

